Z||000000||the need for speed||12-05-2000||11:48 AM||||are all the moog ball joints adjustable or is it just a certain one like the front upper,front lower,or rear bottom.because i called carparts.com and the guy said that there moog balljoints were not adjustable.does this guy not know what he is talking about ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-05-2000||11:56 AM||||The MOOG ball joints I bought (thru the Fiero Store) were slotted (adjustable) for the upper ones. The bottoms were not adjustable.<BR>I have had bad luck with carparts.com and wrenchhead.com<BR>The only reason I ordered the ball joints from the Fiero Store was I bought the entire KYB suspension kit, Ball Joints, Tierod ends, poly bushings, rotors and bearings (front and back) at one time. When it was all done I probably saved about $10.00 and had all the parts 4 days later.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||12-05-2000||12:20 PM||||Oreif is right. Only the front upper ball joints can be "adjustable." If they have slots (elongated bolt holes), then they are adjustable. If they have perfectly round bolt holes, they are not. However, even the "non-adjustable" upper ball joints can be mounted in two positions. Sometimes the alignment technician has to turn the ball joint 180 degrees to allow it to be closer to specs, so in a way, even the non-adjustable ones have two "adjustments." Is that clear as mud?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||12-05-2000||12:59 PM||||Every upper balljoint I've been able to find has been slotted.  I'm pretty sure every manufacturer is using that type..||||reg||1
